      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Predictability often stems from differing workplace cultural norms rather than a fundamental lack of responsibility. In parts of Southeast Asia, relationship-based work styles can sometimes prioritize harmony over strict adherence to immediate schedules. In Sub-Saharan Africa, communication styles may be more indirect, which can be misinterpreted as a lack of commitment or clarity. To mitigate this, success often relies on establishing very clear, documented processes and designated local leadership who can bridge cultural gaps.",
      "source": "target",
