      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. So basically, you're saying that Eastern Europe is the \"default\" for professional autonomy, while the other two regions are more \"high-maintenance\" due to these cultural differences? It feels like you're implying that a manager from the West would find it much harder to trust the professionalism of workers in those regions without constant checking. From a pure ROI perspective, is it fair to say that the \"management overhead\" for Africa and SE Asia makes them inherently more risky or less efficient for high-precision tasks compared to the European labor force?",
