      "content": "Framing it as inherently \"high-maintenance\" might be an oversimplification, but the operational approach differs. European teams generally follow task-oriented, highly structured professional norms, which translates to lower perceived management overhead for routine tasks. For Southeast Asia and Sub-Saharan Africa, the required management focus is often on building interpersonal trust and clarifying expectations, making the initial overhead higher. Whether this translates to lower ROI hinges on whether your high-precision tasks can adapt to the relational management style required in those regions.",
